    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/tool-graph.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The relation is `satisfies`, and it has a direction",
      "prov:value": "That direction is the whole of keeping them apart. Read tool-to-skill it says\n*\"this is one way to do that\"*. Reversed, it would say *\"this skill is a\ntool\"*, which is false and is the conflation the owner named on 2026-09-21:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/tool-graph.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why this page exists at all",
      "prov:value": "The `tools` entry in `cat-harness.json` declared\n`coverage.docs: \"cat-harness/docs/concepts/skills.md\"` until 2026-09-22 — a page titled\n*\"Skills & roles\"*, whose headings are Skills, Roles, and Capabilities &\nrequirements. There was **no tools section in it**. The tools graph had no\ndocumentation of its own and pointed at a page about something else.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/tool-graph.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why this page exists at all",
      "prov:value": "The check in force asks only whether the declared path exists. It did. So\nnothing ever flagged it, and every consumer that counts documented graphs\ncounted this one. It is `pb04` — *a dead link is worse than no link* — one\nlevel up, where the link is not dead at all and simply points somewhere else."
    }
  ]
}
